abstract: >-
  A systematization and empirical comparison of reconstruction attacks against
  synthetic tabular data, including six new attacks (CoBP-RA, CondMST, CondDDPM,
  CondRePaint, ARFFormer and MultiHeadMLP), the composable chaining and
  ensembling wrappers, nine synthetic-data generators plus differentially private
  mechanisms across nine privacy budgets, and a database of 49,126 scored
  attack runs. Insights are drawn in part from the authors' winning entry to the
  NIST Collaborative Research Cycle.
keywords:
  - synthetic data
  - reconstruction attack
  - attribute inference
  - differential privacy
  - privacy-enhancing technologies
  - tabular data
